# YouTube Comment Scraper (Ryan Trahan Dataset)

## Overview

This project is a Python-based YouTube comment scraper that collects top-level comments from videos in a single YouTube channel (default: Ryan Trahan) using the YouTube Data API v3.

The scraper is designed to introduce controlled randomness in video and comment selection so that each run produces a slightly different dataset while remaining focused on the same channel.

It outputs structured CSV files for use in data analysis, machine learning, and natural language processing tasks.

---

## Features

- Scrapes YouTube comments using the official YouTube Data API v3
- Targets a single channel (default: Ryan Trahan)
- Randomized video selection order per run
- Randomized comment ordering per video
- Automatic CSV output generation per run (no overwriting)
- Built-in duplicate removal within each run
- Lightweight and easy to run locally

---

## Requirements

- Python 3.9 or higher
- YouTube Data API v3 key

